    "body": "Hi @flashymittens Thank you for the feedback — that’s a very good point.\n\nI agree that “name validation” can be extremely complex across different languages and cultures. My initial idea was more about enabling browser-level declarative validation hooks (e.g., validation=\"name\", validation=\"phone\", etc.), not necessarily enforcing strict built-in patterns.\n\nInstead of rigid validation logic, the attribute could define standardized presets or declarative behaviors, for example:\n\nvalidation=\"name\" → allows developers to specify a custom pattern + localized error message with native browser UI handling\n\nvalidation=\"custom\" → could reference a JSON-like schema defined inside a <script type=\"validation\"> block for advanced use cases\n\nThe broader goal is to reduce boilerplate JavaScript and make validation more consistent, accessible, and beginner-friendly, while still keeping flexibility for complex or localized data types.\n\nI’d be happy to collaborate further or prototype refinements if that would help clarify the idea. \n",
